= Question 34

The graph of a rational function\, $f \(x \)$\, has a point of discontinuity when $x = 2 $ and an asymptote

when $x = 4 $. Write a possible equation for $f \(x \)$.

== Solution

A possible equation is:

$  f \(x \)= frac(x - 2 ,\(x - 2 \)\(x - 4 \))  $

